From: Remy <remy@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] aarch64: run the watchdog handoff from kmain after BOOTSTRAP install

Second gate catch (P3-fix gate round 2, 2026-11-01): the
0045 placement in arch start() STILL panicked with
"BOOTSTRAP was not set". args.bootstrap() only builds the
Bootstrap value; the BOOTSTRAP spin::Once is installed by
BOOTSTRAP.call_once() inside kmain (src/startup/mod.rs),
after secondary-CPU init and scheme globals. So the first
point init_env() may legally be read is inside kmain,
immediately after that call_once - which is where the
handoff now runs (cfg target_arch=aarch64 + feature).
Userspace has not started; the healthy-point argument is
unchanged. 0045's start() call is removed; the pointer
comments in device/mod.rs and the qcom_wdt module doc are
corrected to the kmain placement. Recorded plainly: root's
0045 evidence summary misstated where the Once installs,
and the Muse Wonder consult (spark-out/
wonder-p3fix-consult.md) repeated the same assumption from
that summary while agreeing with the root cause - the
emulator gate is the ground truth and outranked both.

Agent: Remy (root of record)
Model: Muse Wonder (muse-wonder-1.0)
Provider: Meta

---
diff --git a/src/arch/aarch64/device/mod.rs b/src/arch/aarch64/device/mod.rs
index 57ee7eea..5a8ef016 100644
--- a/src/arch/aarch64/device/mod.rs
+++ b/src/arch/aarch64/device/mod.rs
@@ -65,10 +65,10 @@ pub unsafe fn init_devicetree(fdt: &Fdt) {
         info!("RTC INIT");
         rtc::init(fdt);
         // The APSS watchdog handoff (qcom_wdt::handoff, patch 0043)
-        // runs from arch start() right after args.bootstrap(): it
-        // reads REDOX_WDT_MODE via crate::startup::init_env(), which
-        // panics before the bootstrap environment is installed
-        // (patch 0045; the first 0043 gate run panicked here).
+        // runs from kmain() immediately after BOOTSTRAP is
+        // installed: it reads REDOX_WDT_MODE via
+        // crate::startup::init_env(), which panics anywhere earlier
+        // (patches 0045/0046; the first 0043 gate run panicked here).
     }
 }
 
diff --git a/src/arch/aarch64/device/qcom_wdt.rs b/src/arch/aarch64/device/qcom_wdt.rs
index 9c6fb6b5..d41a242a 100644
--- a/src/arch/aarch64/device/qcom_wdt.rs
+++ b/src/arch/aarch64/device/qcom_wdt.rs
@@ -8,8 +8,8 @@
 //! servicing stops at handoff, so an armed watchdog bites ~32 s into
 //! the boot unless the kernel takes ownership (REVIEW-20261031-2230
 //! F-4). This module is that handoff. Once device init is complete
-//! and the bootstrap environment exists (arch start(), just before
-//! kmain; patch 0045) it either DISARMS the watchdog (normal images; the TTL/reset
+//! and the bootstrap environment exists (kmain(), immediately after
+//! BOOTSTRAP is installed; patches 0045/0046) it either DISARMS the watchdog (normal images; the TTL/reset
 //! machinery owns the timeline from there) or deliberately LEAVES it
 //! armed (stall-test images, whose bite must land in the installed
 //! system — the early download-mode cookie clear, patch 0042, makes
diff --git a/src/arch/aarch64/start.rs b/src/arch/aarch64/start.rs
index ab35f6da..5cd0b32d 100644
--- a/src/arch/aarch64/start.rs
+++ b/src/arch/aarch64/start.rs
@@ -136,15 +136,6 @@ unsafe extern "C" fn start(args_ptr: *const KernelArgs) -> ! {
             args.bootstrap()
         };
 
-        // P3 F-4 (REVIEW-20261031-2230): take ownership of the
-        // bootloader-armed APSS watchdog. Device init is complete
-        // and the bootstrap environment now exists - the earliest
-        // point qcom_wdt::handoff() may read REDOX_WDT_MODE via
-        // crate::startup::init_env() (it panics before
-        // args.bootstrap() installs it; patch 0045). Still before
-        // kmain/userspace: the healthy point for this phase.
-        #[cfg(feature = "qcom-wdt-handoff")]
-        device::qcom_wdt::handoff();
 
         // TODO: use stack
         crate::startup::kmain(bootstrap, Kstack::new().expect("failed to allocate stack"));
diff --git a/src/startup/mod.rs b/src/startup/mod.rs
index 4ab58897..d3c20969 100644
--- a/src/startup/mod.rs
+++ b/src/startup/mod.rs
@@ -191,6 +191,17 @@ pub(crate) fn kmain(bootstrap: Bootstrap, kmain_kstack: Kstack) -> ! {
 
     BOOTSTRAP.call_once(|| bootstrap);
 
+    // P3 F-4 (REVIEW-20261031-2230): take ownership of the
+    // bootloader-armed APSS watchdog. This is the first point
+    // crate::startup::init_env() may be read - the BOOTSTRAP
+    // Once is installed immediately above - and userspace has
+    // not started: the healthy point for this phase. (0043 put
+    // the call at the end of device init and 0045 in arch
+    // start(); both panic on the unset Once - the environment
+    // exists only from here on.)
+    #[cfg(all(target_arch = "aarch64", feature = "qcom-wdt-handoff"))]
+    crate::arch::device::qcom_wdt::handoff();
+
     profiling::ready_for_profiling();
 
     let owner = None; // kmain not owned by any fd
